**7. Recursive shape testing**

**PROVED — cost substitution.** If a rigorously available factoring algorithm factors integers of size \(\sqrt p\) with constant \(c_{\rm fac}/\sqrt2\), replace (1) by
\[
\min_{a>0}\max\left\{
a+\frac{c_{\rm fac}}{\sqrt2},\;
a+\frac{\theta}{2a},\;
Ca
\right\}.
\tag{22}
\]
A DL algorithm alone is not a factoring subroutine, so this substitution requires an actual factoring algorithm.

**SPECULATIVE — common recursive bound.** If one justified a common recursive factoring bound and retained quadratic post-processing, the familiar formal fixed point is
\[
c=\sqrt{(1+\sqrt2)\theta}.
\]
At \(\theta\downarrow3/10\), this is approximately \(0.8510\). It requires a separate recursive analysis; it does not follow merely from the DL reduction.
